Here are 35 real-world issues I’ve faced in production (and how to fix them) 👇

⸻

⚙️ POD & CONTAINER ISSUES
1️⃣ CrashLoopBackOff → kubectl logs <pod> -p
2️⃣ ImagePullBackOff → Wrong image or registry auth issue
3️⃣ ErrImagePull → Invalid image path/tag
4️⃣ OOMKilled → Increase memory limits
5️⃣ ContainerCreating forever → PVC not bound or pull delay
6️⃣ Init Container Failed → Missing config or dependency
7️⃣ Pod Stuck Terminating → Finalizer/mount issue → --grace-period=0
8️⃣ Completed Pods not cleaned → CronJob history limits
9️⃣ Pod in Unknown state → Node unreachable
🔟 Back-off restarting container → App crash loop

⸻

🧠 SCHEDULING & NODE ISSUES
11️⃣ Pod Pending → No node resources or taint mismatch
12️⃣ Node NotReady → Kubelet or CNI issue
13️⃣ Evicted Pods → Disk/memory pressure
14️⃣ Unschedulable Pod → Wrong affinity/selector
15️⃣ High CPU Usage → kubectl top nodes/pods
16️⃣ DiskPressure Warning → Clear /var/lib/docker
17️⃣ Node NotFound → Re-register kubelet
18️⃣ Taint/Toleration conflict → Fix mismatched tolerations

⸻

🌐 NETWORKING & SERVICE ISSUES
19️⃣ Service Not Reachable → Check endpoints
20️⃣ DNS Resolution Failure → Inspect CoreDNS logs
21️⃣ LoadBalancer Pending → Cloud provider or MetalLB misconfig
22️⃣ Ingress 404/503 → Rule/path mismatch
23️⃣ NetworkPolicy blocking → kubectl describe networkpolicy
24️⃣ Pod-to-Pod communication failed → Check CNI plugin
25️⃣ Port-forward failure → Local firewall or proxy issue
26️⃣ Service IP Conflict → CIDR overlap

⸻

💾 STORAGE & CONFIG ISSUES
27️⃣ PVC Pending → Misconfigured StorageClass
28️⃣ ReadOnly filesystem → SecurityContext issue
29️⃣ ConfigMap not mounted → Wrong path or key
30️⃣ Secret mount failed → Invalid base64
31️⃣ PersistentVolume unavailable → NFS/EBS backend issue

⸻

📊 MONITORING & CONTROL PLANE ISSUES
32️⃣ Metrics Missing → metrics-server not running
33️⃣ API Server Down → ETCD overload
34️⃣ Kubelet Crash → System resource exhaustion
35️⃣ ETCD Disk Full → API latency, monitor /var/lib/etcd

⸻

💡 Pro Tip:
Run this before anything else 👇
kubectl describe <resource> — It tells you the whole story.

Troubleshooting Kubernetes isn’t about memorizing commands — it’s about understanding how all layers connect.
Break things. Fix them. Learn every time. 🔥
